+# Bridge jumps - 2026-10-16
+
+The owner asked for bridge release, found the initial jumps exaggerated, then found the reduced version invisible. Final tuning restores a visible short hop: bounded suspension rebound up to 3.2 m/s, game-scale gravity of 22 m/s squared, and less than 0.3 seconds of airtime in the tested standard crossings. At 24-36 m/s, 32 m spans lift roughly 22-24 cm; the shortest 24 m high-speed spans lift about 6.8 cm. At 3 m/s the car stays planted. These are controlled desktop measurements; owner feel remains the acceptance test.
+
+BJ01 covers canonical release/landing, BJ02 restrained native motion/shared support/ghosts, and BJ03 exact replay/rewind/reset/version isolation. Existing G01/R01/Q01 remain.
+
+Release samples the same front/rear axle support used by the visible car. A bounded suspension rebound keeps the hop readable when a short crest loses its slope within one tick. Release waits for axle support to flatten. An eight-step landing probe gradually reduces strength on short decks, replacing the overly strict veto that hid the jump. A 24-tick landing cooldown prevents repeated skips at one crest. Descending ramps receive no separate launch impulse.
+
+Airborne movement carries planar and angular momentum without tyre steering or pedal force. Height integrates in world space against the changing deck support. Landing dissipates bounded speed and feeds the existing suspension. Existing jump hazards retain their original integration. Racing suppresses the old independent cosmetic lift, retaining the ground pitch spring. Reverse flight pitch and personal ghosts agree; rewind markers use axle support. Actual road/bridge meshes, collision rails/layers, underpasses, camera and cache bounds remain. The race and finish coasting reuse the prepared immutable sampler; other simulations prepare once per bridged track. Tracks without bridges allocate none.
+
+The bridge slice introduces physics arcade-planar-0.63. Concurrent work advances the shared source/assertion to 0.64, which is preserved. The task-only checkpoint isolates the 0.63 change; final source hashes and staged verifier use shared 0.64. The outer 24-entry snapshot and input/proof schemas remain; the nested jump tuple adds bridge_airborne. Property-based rewind retains it. The verifier stages the new helper. Historical physics0.50/rules20 and existing boards remain unchanged; matching rollout is separate.
+
+Actual validation with pinned Godot 4.7.2 and isolated APPDATA:
+
+- Final headless, Compatibility and Mobile: 430 checks each, zero failures. All five axle sizes, 45 crossings, both directions/backing, slow contact, world-space arcs, ignored air controls, every-tick JSON replay, midflight rewind/reset, twelve short/long/rotated cases, actual game presentation, duplicate-draw stability and landing compression pass.
+- Native captures: [Compatibility](evidence/bridge-jumps-2026-10-16/jump-gl_compatibility.png), [Mobile](evidence/bridge-jumps-2026-10-16/jump-mobile.png). These are scripted practice frames with synthetic frame timing, not FPS evidence.
+- During tuning, bridge contacts16, checkpoint layers259, entry258, exit2527, rewind61 and driving72 pass. Actual five-lap Dust cloud races finish at29139 then29097 ticks; Over and under at25805 then25712 ticks. These larger runs precede the final axle-flattening refinement; final focused runs test the exact final tuning. Whole-project parser passes837 scripts during the iteration.
+- Suspension assertions59 pass headless and Compatibility, but teardown reports leaked renderer resources. Their clean-exit commands remain unsuccessful; no cleanup fix is claimed.
+- Initial isolated verifier suite:68 passed/2 failed. A new ghost reference depended on a constant absent from archived physics0.50; a direct helper preload fixes it. Final archived replay/current-version tests both pass. An intermediate concurrent0.64 versus staged0.63 mismatch is retained, then resolved by refreshing the isolated snapshot. The unrelated HTTP fixture expects14 checks while its isolated client prints13 checks/zero failures; that assertion and client remain unchanged.
+
+Retained initial diagnostics include Windows certificate/log sandbox restrictions, invalid oversized paint, test controls held after landing, the archived helper dependency, and a premature tiny Kart skip fixed by waiting for axle support to flatten. Both earlier4.5m/s and1.5m/s settings are superseded. A Windows encoding error truncated AGENTS during documentation writing; it was restored from the latest task backup plus the exact newer photo-override patch. All unaffected restored sections were compared exactly; final writes use explicit UTF-8.
+
+[report.json](evidence/bridge-jumps-2026-10-16/report.json) records commands/logs, hashes, limitations and the isolated review patch. Owner/physical-phone driving feel and matching client/verifier rollout remain. No phone attachment check/test, APK, live backend mutation or deployment was performed by this task.
